    "definition": "Minimum Kakeya set in F31^3, specified by one arbitrary affine line in each of993 projective directions. Taking union does not restrict the minimum: every Kakeya set contains such a choice and its union is no larger. No quadratic-template restriction in formal candidate domain.",
    "human_source": "Classical odd-field quadratic residue construction as recorded in Bukh-Chao2021 section4. Root independently generates its membership predicate on all29791 points and matches human line union exactly:8641 =30*16^2+31^2.",
    "public_reference": "Station/Dualverse Chung-Du-Wesley2608.23691v2 section6.1 S1 equation1, AI-generated construction. Root independently builds the quadratic membership set plus the rational one-pole plane boundary; formula(2p^3+7p^2+3)/8 gives8289 at31 and matches saved reference line union exactly. First-party notebook and paper archived. Non-primary8288 claim excluded; AlphaEvolve8290 remains a separately scoped un-reproduced report.",
    "open_status": "Bukh-Chao leading constant1/4 is asymptotically sharp, not an exact finite31 optimum. Finite reported lower bound ceil(31^5/61^2)=7694, arithmetic recomputed; underlying general theorem cited. Station section6.1 explicitly leaves lower-order corrections open. No same-parameter optimality proof located.",
    "independent_method": "Root projectivizes all29790 nonzero vectors and obtains993 directions, then iterates modular additions into a dense29791-byte bitmap. Formal checker uses a prescribed chart and sets of t-times-direction triples. Additional independent full-space membership reconstruction verifies both external formulas.",
    "initial_search_and_admission": "Standalone all-lines-through-origin seed29791. Own generic baseline17574 and evolution15534; external human8641/reference8289 never read by candidate searches. All five strict runs, claim-invariant complete checker returns, duplicate-direction damage, replay, cold export and error/nonfinite/timeout controls passed."
